---
# architecture.md section 8's CI/CD table: ".clang-tidy -- Not yet configured." This is that
# configuration, wired into CI the same way the `format` job already gates on .clang-format.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: bug-finding and performance checks, not style/naming (clang-
# format plus this project's own documented conventions, section 11.2, already cover that -- a
# readability-identifier-naming config duplicating them would just be a second place for the two
# to drift). WarningsAsErrors matches every other structural check in this project (section 2.2's
# size caps, section 2.3's layer rules): hard failure, never a warning that nobody reads.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  modernize-use-nullptr,
  modernize-use-override,
  modernize-use-equals-default,
  modernize-use-equals-delete,
  cppcoreguidelines-slicing,
  cppcoreguidelines-special-member-functions,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -performance-for-range-copy

# performance-for-range-copy fires on `for (auto [x, y] : registry.view<...>().each())` --
# structured-binding-by-value is the iteration idiom every system in modes/space/systems/ already
# uses (dozens of call sites, architecture.md section 11.3's own system-recipe example among
# them). Switching to `const auto&` per the check's suggested fix is very likely a real, safe
# micro-optimization (entt's each() hands back live component references, not temporaries), but
# rewriting an established idiom across the whole systems/ tree is a mechanical cleanup PR of its
# own, not something to fold into "configure clang-tidy in CI." Excluded here; worth a follow-up
# issue if it turns out to matter at profiled scale.
WarningsAsErrors: "*"

# Only this project's own headers -- not EnTT/raylib/nlohmann_json's, which vcpkg installs and
# this project does not control.
HeaderFilterRegex: "^.*/src/.*"

FormatStyle: none
